  there exist $l$ polynomials satisfying the same conditions with $J'$ and $I'$
  replaced by $J$ and $I$, respectively. For each $i\le l$, there is $q_i$
  in the extension of $I'$ so that $p_i' = p_i+q_i \in J$. 
